msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/procs/executables.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.procs.executables.is_executable_in_posix:11
msgid ""
"If ``False`` do not check that file exists. This made to consistency with "
"``is_executable_in_windows``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/procs/executables.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.procs.executables.is_executable_in_windows:2
msgid "Check the file is executable in Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/procs/executables.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.procs.executables.is_executable_in_windows:11
msgid ""
"If ``False`` do not check that file exists. This helps to disable double "
"checking in case the file already checked in upstream code. This is "
"important for Windows where checking can take a long time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/procs/executables.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.procs.executables.is_file:2
msgid "Check that ``filepath`` is file and exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/procs/executables.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.procs.executables.locate_executable:2
msgid "Search executable binary name in ``$PATH`` and return full path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/procs/executables.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.procs.executables.locate_file:2
msgid ""
"Search file name in the current working directory and in ``$PATH`` and "
"return full path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/procs/executables.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.procs.executables.locate_file_in_path_env:2
msgid "Search file name in ``$PATH`` and return full path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/procs/executables.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.procs.executables.locate_file_in_path_env:4
msgid ""
"Compromise. There is no way to get case sensitive file name without listing "
"all files. If the file name is ``CaMeL.exe`` and we found that ``camel.EXE`` "
"exists there is no way to get back the case sensitive name. We don't want to "
"read the list of files in all ``$PATH`` directories because of performance "
"reasons. So we're ok to get existent but case insensitive (or different) "
"result from resolver. May be in the future file systems as well as Python "
"Path will be smarter to get the case sensitive name. The task for reading "
"and returning case sensitive filename we give to completer in interactive "
"mode with ``commands_cache``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/procs/executables.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.procs.executables.locate_relative_path:2
msgid "Return absolute path by relative file path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/procs/executables.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.procs.executables.locate_relative_path:4
msgid ""
"We should not locate files without prefix (e.g. ``\"binfile\"``) by security "
"reasons like other shells. If directory has \"binfile\" it can be called "
"only by providing prefix \"./binfile\" explicitly."
msgstr ""
